swer within \\boxed{}.\nuser\nReturn your final response within \\boxed{}. In the diagram below, $\\overline{AB}\\parallel \\overline{CD}$ and $\\angle AXE$ is $108^\\circ$ less than 3 times $\\angle CYX$.  Find $\\angle BXY$.\n\n[asy]\n\nunitsize(1inch);\n\npair A,B,C,D,X,Y,EE,F;\n\nA = (0,0);\n\nB=(1,0);\n\nC = (0,0.8);\n\nD=(1,0.8);\n\nEE = (0.35,-0.3);\n\nF = (0.8,1.1);\n\ndraw(EE--F);\n\ndraw(A--B);\n\ndraw(C--D);\n\ndot(A);\n\ndot(B);\n\ndot(C);\n\ndot(D);\n\ndot(EE);\n\ndot(F);\n\nlabel(\"$E$\",EE,S);\n\nlabel(\"$F$\",F,N);\n\nX = intersectionpoint(A--B,EE--F);\n\nY = intersectionpoint(C--D,EE--F);\n\nlabel(\"$X$\",X,NNW);\n\nlabel(\"$Y$\",Y,NNW);\n\nlabel(\"$A$\",A,W);\n\nlabel(\"$B$\",B,E);\n\nlabel(\"$C$\",C,W);\n\nlabel(\"$D$\",D,E);\n\ndot(X);\n\ndot(Y);\n\n[/asy]\nassistant\n", "response": "Since \\(\\overline{AB} \\parallel \\overline{CD}\\), we know that \\(\\angle AXE\\) and \\(\\angle CYX\\) are corresponding angles. Therefore, \\(\\angle AXE = \\angle CYX\\).\n\nLet \\(\\angle CYX = x\\). Then, \\(\\angle AXE = x\\).\n\nAccording to the problem, \\(\\angle AXE\\) is \\(108^\\circ\\) less than 3 times \\(\\angle CYX\\). This can be written as:\n\\[\n\\angle AXE = 3x - 108^\\circ\n\\]\n\nSince \\(\\angle AXE = x\\), we can set up the equation:\n\\[\nx = 3x - 108^\\circ\n\\]\n\nTo solve for \\(x\\), we rearrange the equation:\n\\[\nx - 3x = -108^\\circ\n\\]\n\\[\n-2x = -108^\\circ\n\\]\n\\[\nx = 54^\\circ\n\\]\n\nThus, \\(\\angle CYX = 54^\\circ\\).\n\nSince \\(\\angle BXY\\) and \\(\\angle CYX\\) are corresponding angles and \\(\\overline{AB} \\parallel \\overline{CD}\\), \\(\\angle BXY = \\angle CYX\\).\n\nTherefore, \\(\\angle BXY = 54^\\circ\\).\n\nThe final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{54}\n\\]"}, {"prompt": "system\nPlease reason step by step, and put your final answer within \\boxed{}.\nuser\nReturn your final response within \\boxed{}. In the diagram below, $\\overline{AB}\\parallel \\overline{CD}$ and $\\angle AXE$ is $108^\\circ$ less than 3 tim